2026-08-25T00:00:00Z (RFD66606-1027) 'GPU tier per model
 # uuid: 3a6defc4-14de-5080-aeed-0e5587a4ec9a
 # tags: rfd:title, rfd:flight-level:l2, rfd:attest-in:none
 RFD:Committed  1 RFD
 Serials:Weftspun

2026-08-25T00:00:01Z (RFD66606-1027) 'capacity planning
 # tags: rfd:feature, rfd:no-final-newline
 Text:RFD1027  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:02Z (RFD66606-1027) 'Each model gets its own GPU tier, sized alone and not as part of a set.
 # tags: rfd:hook
 Text:RFD1027  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:03Z (RFD66606-1027) 'Does every model fit one device at once? This RFD first summed 116.45 GB against a 128 GB DGX Spark, found about 10 GB of headroom, and called the margin too small.
 # tags: rfd:intrigue
 Text:RFD1027  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:04Z (RFD66606-1027) 'Size a new model alone against the weights RFD66606-1025 gives and its activation peak, then place it in the tier table below.
 # tags: rfd:exit
 Text:RFD1027  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:05Z (RFD66606-1027) 'GPU tier per model
 # tags: rfd:details-title, rfd:no-final-newline
 Text:RFD1027  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:06Z (RFD66606-1027) 'Size each model on its own. The question is which GPU tier one model needs, and not whether a set of models co-resides.
 # tags: rfd:decision
 Text:RFD1027  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:07Z (RFD66606-1027) 'Two numbers decide the tier: the weights RFD66606-1025 gives per model, and the activation peak, which depends on the resolution and the batch size.
 # tags: rfd:decision
 Text:RFD1027  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:08Z (RFD66606-1027) 'Every model in the catalog reaches a 24 GB card. The workspace standardizes on **QAFT 4-bit** as the default weights format where upstream ships one (Gemma-4-12B QAT Q4_0 is the canonical example and reasoning core per RFD66606-2169). Models without a QAFT release run at published precision (bf16) with staged loading.
 # tags: rfd:decision
 Text:RFD1027  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:09Z (RFD66606-1027) 'RFD66606-1025 gives the arithmetic and the memory per model. RFD66606-1036 gives the packaging that sets the tier.
 # tags: rfd:related
 Text:RFD1027  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:10Z (RFD66606-1027) 'Tier per model
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD1027  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:11Z (RFD66606-1027) 'A tier must hold the weights and the activations together. Format is QAFT 4-bit where upstream ships one; bf16 otherwise. Peak is the resident weight set, smaller than total for staged models.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD1027  1 LINE
 Text:Written

